h} :answer/value "{y}^{2}-81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483186} :answer-field/id #uuid "7fe3c06a-aa72-5539-944a-6186ddc1f026" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483287}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bb3555b9-96c6-521f-8784-a2e30e2526a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-61979" :question/problem "$(y-9)(y+9)=$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n(a+b)(a-b)={a}^{2}-{b}^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=y$ and $b=9,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-9)(y+9) & = \\\\ {y}^{2}-{9}^{2} & = \\\\ {y}^{2}-81.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483405 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12b23156-098d-5b78-902a-2222d96e3b63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{a}^{3}+2{a}^{2}+8a+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482844} {:answer/id #uuid "6b196904-d748-541e-b99e-230895127da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{a}^{3}+3{a}^{2}+21a+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482997} {:answer/id #uuid "a3fcfd07-2220-5f18-914f-b4ca1f9aeeb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{a}^{3}+6{a}^{2}+7a+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483090} {:answer/id #uuid "c182dc2e-15df-545b-94cd-d81d50cc6098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{a}^{3}+{a}^{2}+a+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483136} {:answer/id #uuid "f2d4cb32-66b1-5b59-b9f2-a318636d096d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{a}^{3}+5{a}^{2}+14a+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b196904-d748-541e-b99e-230895127da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{a}^{3}+3{a}^{2}+21a+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482997} :answer-field/id #uuid "997df8e8-e4cd-59a3-9c85-60df68b6ea05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c0098ac0-7ed8-5f08-8d20-947c580b7f8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-78165" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $(2a+1)({a}^{2}+a+10)?$" :question/worked-solution "We distribute both terms of the binomial in the first set of parentheses to the trinomial in the second set of parentheses. Then, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2a+1)({a}^{2}+a+10) & = \\\\ 2a({a}^{2}+a+10)+1({a}^{2}+a+10) & = \\\\ 2{a}^{3}+2{a}^{2}+20a+{a}^{2}+a+10 & = \\\\ 2{a}^{3}+3{a}^{2}+21a+10\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483415 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "906a0b55-204a-56a6-a903-6f001989e184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "906a0b55-204a-56a6-a903-6f001989e184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483062} :answer-field/id #uuid "15fd5e31-0a26-515f-9010-378807b928a9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483247} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "236446a4-7281-5c03-903f-c5084de03781" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "236446a4-7281-5c03-903f-c5084de03781" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482875} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d81b9e9-cd19-5eec-9e3c-c8f9eb596d52" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483281} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18be1f63-741d-5018-91f5-2810be8a6b0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18be1f63-741d-5018-91f5-2810be8a6b0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482859} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b2c159e-029b-5def-beed-5f2e79c867bd" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483295}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d54b0636-ad05-55a6-91c9-9613b500f9d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-224935" :question/problem "Factor the following quadratic expression.\n\n$5{b}^{2}-34b-7=(b\\,-$\n{{field-1}}$)($\n{{field-2}}$b\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "We must factor the quadratic expression\n\n$$\n5{b}^{2}-34b-7.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find two numbers that \n\n- multiply to the product of the quadratic coefficient and the constant ($5\\times -7=-35$), and\n\n- add to the linear coefficient ($-34$).\n\nFirst, we find the factor pairs of $-35:$\n\n$$\n(1,-35),\\,(-1,35),\\,(5,-7),\\,(-5,7)\n$$\n\nNotice the numbers in the factor pair $(1,-35)$ add to $-34:$ \n\n$$\n1+(-35)=-34\\,✓\n$$\n\nThen, rewrite the linear term as $b-35b,$ and factor the result by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{b}^{2}-34b-7 & = \\\\ 5{b}^{2}+b-35b-7 & = \\\\ (5{b}^{2}+b)-(35b+7) & = \\\\ b(5b+1)-7(5b+1) & = \\\\ (b-7)(5b+1) & \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483417 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74aecbb6-b8e5-5ebd-857f-df6f9036c234" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483013} {:answer/id #uuid "913d3085-e6ae-5f6f-898a-07d1e1175573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483067} {:answer/id #uuid "d509cae9-f2bc-5f3b-ac9d-5abef902b561" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483171} {:answer/id #uuid "e0fd4e23-d57a-5ac8-b610-7ece1ba4ab1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483191} {:answer/id #uuid "fd942ed2-02f2-5c55-b087-0fd2363dcdd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74aecbb6-b8e5-5ebd-857f-df6f9036c234" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483013} :answer-field/id #uuid "f11bf0b1-7d95-5083-be12-730d1dee4129" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483335}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d7c22bb7-72a0-576c-8d37-5df7a0b2d33e" :question/math-academy-id "q-78175" :question/problem "Given that  $({s}^{2}+2s-1)({s}^{2}-s+2)={s}^{4}+a{s}^{3}+b{s}^{2}+cs-2,$ calculate $a+b+c.$" :question/worked-solution "We distribute all three terms of the trinomial in the first set of parentheses to the trinomial in the second set of parentheses. Then, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({s}^{2}+2s-1)({s}^{2}-s+2) & = \\\\ {s}^{2}({s}^{2}-s+2)+2s({s}^{2}-s+2)-1({s}^{2}-s+2) & = \\\\ {s}^{4}-{s}^{3}+2{s}^{2}+2{s}^{3}-2{s}^{2}+4s-{s}^{2}+s-2 & = \\\\ {s}^{4}+{s}^{3}-{s}^{2}+5s-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,$ $b=-1,$ and $c=5.$ So, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+(-1)+5=5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483423 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6861b754-7244-526a-bb95-db4bb52ba278" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36{y}^{2}-36y-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482992} {:answer/id #uuid "6ada63d2-f554-569d-adf8-851cac7fd0c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36{y}^{2}+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482996} {:answer/id #uuid "89cb1df2-e524-5570-9838-bdd99a2d88d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36{y}^{2}-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483053} {:answer/id #uuid "f222be28-aefa-5ea1-ae26-55a00d649b12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36{y}^{2}-36y+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483219} {:answer/id #uuid "f8de2013-753a-599d-accc-a03d56128aa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36{y}^{2}-18y-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89cb1df2-e524-5570-9838-bdd99a2d88d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36{y}^{2}-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483053} :answer-field/id #uuid "5504c2ee-bec5-5b15-8822-625b2d0c8450" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483267}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e564aec0-fea4-5f31-8155-02342652a572" :question/math-academy-id "q-52172" :question/problem "$(6y+3)(6y-3)=$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n(a+b)(a-b)={a}^{2}-{b}^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=6y$ and $b=3,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6y+3)(6y-3) & = \\\\ (6y)^{2}-{3}^{2} & = \\\\ 36{y}^{2}-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483427 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "043b906f-a914-598a-9f91-5ca6fcec0a3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482815} {:answer/id #uuid "234ba434-25d1-5f9f-b0f4-93fdd591f9c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482874} {:answer/id #uuid "45da7d3c-cb8c-5c94-8b92-1b817b5a7a63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482934} {:answer/id #uuid "70ae1955-aef8-599b-9edf-0669967c6133" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483008} {:answer/id #uuid "afcb38cd-b552-5548-a076-654fa26d9cec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afcb38cd-b552-5548-a076-654fa26d9cec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483109} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2072f7a-cde2-54db-a02e-520c47dd2afc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "efb60196-718e-5a66-900b-f5c4e1c9517a" :question/math-academy-id "q-78178" :question/problem "Given that  $({t}^{2}-6t+9)({t}^{2}-4t+4)={t}^{4}+a{t}^{3}+b{t}^{2}+ct+36,$ calculate $a+b+c.$" :question/worked-solution "We distribute all three terms of the trinomial in the first set of parentheses to the trinomial in the second set of parentheses. Then, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({t}^{2}-6t+9)({t}^{2}-4t+4) & = \\\\ {t}^{2}({t}^{2}-4t+4)+(-6t)({t}^{2}-4t+4)+9({t}^{2}-4t+4) & = \\\\ {t}^{4}-4{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}-6{t}^{3}+24{t}^{2}-24t+9{t}^{2}-36t+36 & = \\\\ {t}^{4}-10{t}^{3}+37{t}^{2}-60t+36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-10,$ $b=37,$ and $c=-60.$ So, \n\n$$\na+b+c=-10+37+(-60)=-33.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483428 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84904924-5125-563e-b3fa-acb7b0f7daef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49-t^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84904924-5125-563e-b3fa-acb7b0f7daef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49-t^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483043} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e9a4ccb-30bc-5597-a94d-6a4016c4f4cc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483245}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f31bb0dc-4f18-5dd8-8c4d-ef7d0360e3ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-237261" :question/problem "Expand the following product.\n\n$(7-t)(7+t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We will use the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n(a+b)(a-b)={a}^{2}-{b}^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=7$ and $b=t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(7-t)(7+t) & = \\\\ {7}^{2}-{t}^{2} & = \\\\ 49-{t}^{2} & .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483429 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "111e1e23-33ab-5eb5-be89-a0516b2a0f95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482838} {:answer/id #uuid "1ec5b16b-b497-5100-aef7-c6132ee98485" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482870} {:answer/id #uuid "9e80e679-f6b4-5b04-9218-ed350b2a908a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483078} {:answer/id #uuid "c7d48439-0e03-55e0-b331-25d7d27150ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483145} {:answer/id #uuid "dafcd1fb-53a4-534a-b4b7-54b36e312d96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e80e679-f6b4-5b04-9218-ed350b2a908a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483078} :answer-field/id #uuid "b05f2dfd-a721-5b93-9f30-acb8924f6d69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483306}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f713a7bd-9c0b-5d5c-8fbb-e0cb95a59072" :question/math-academy-id "q-110877" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\sqrt{3x+5y}$ when $x=1$ and $y=5.$" :question/worked-solution "We replace $x$ with $1$ and $y$ with $5$ in the given expression, and simplify as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3x+5y} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{3(1)+5(5)} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{3+25} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{28} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4\\cdot 7} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{2}^{2}\\cdot 7} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{2}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{7} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483430 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0617ff8b-9a53-5a85-9776-ca14a6b5a1e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5m+1)(m+4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482821} {:answer/id #uuid "3f3f1441-07e1-5f0d-b9d6-5cbf147a0251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5m+4)(2m+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482919} {:answer/id #uuid "a9dba60b-09d4-5767-814a-20971c8a355a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(5m+2)(m+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483099} {:answer/id #uuid "c51f24dc-3a4d-52e8-b926-ba0e14c2c0e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10m+1)(m+4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483140} {:answer/id #uuid "d5ca640d-8f6e-53a9-b58a-e4f953665ac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(5m+1)(m+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f3f1441-07e1-5f0d-b9d6-5cbf147a0251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5m+4)(2m+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482919} :answer-field/id #uuid "baaf1380-7960-5d0a-861f-dfdf49029a8a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f8a011fe-bff7-586f-86e9-fabb797df0e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-111838" :question/problem "$10{m}^{2}+13m+4=$" :question/worked-solution "We must factor the quadratic expression\n\n$$\n10{m}^{2}+13m+4.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find two numbers that \n\n- multiply to the product of the quadratic coefficient and the constant ($10\\times 4=40$), and\n\n- add to the linear coefficient ($13$).\n\nSince all coefficients are positive, we only need to consider the positive factor pairs of $40.$\n\nThe positive factor pairs of $40$ are\n\n$$\n(1,40),\\,(2,20),\\,(4,10),\\,(5,8).\n$$\n\nNotice the numbers in the factor pair $(5,8)$ add to $13:$ \n\n$$\n5+8=13\\,✓\n$$\n\nThen, we write the linear term as $5m+8m,$ and factor the result by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10{m}^{2}+13m+4 & = \\\\ 10{m}^{2}+5m+8m+4 & = \\\\ (10{m}^{2}+5m)+(8m+4) & = \\\\ 5m(2m+1)+4(2m+1) & = \\\\ (5m+4)(2m+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484207 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2c0111b-77f9-5dd6-b35b-60f59cc17ed0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{4}+5y^{2}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2c0111b-77f9-5dd6-b35b-60f59cc17ed0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{4}+5y^{2}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483951} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8ce49c6-f3b3-587c-9376-29dad2462846" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484166}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3049a347-62dd-59fc-b924-9cdaded3eea2" :question/math-academy-id "q-236407" :question/problem "Given that $f(y)={y}^{4}+3{y}^{2}-1$ and $g(y)=2{y}^{2}-3,$ write $f(y)+g(y)$ in **standard form**.\n\n$f(y)+g(y)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We put a plus sign between the two polynomials, collect like terms, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(y)+g(y) & = \\\\ ({y}^{4}+3{y}^{2}-1)+(2{y}^{2}-3) & = \\\\ {y}^{4}+3{y}^{2}-1+2{y}^{2}-3 & = \\\\ {y}^{4}+(3+2){y}^{2}+(-1-3) & = \\\\ {y}^{4}+5{y}^{2}-4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484210 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c3ae2ef-052d-59ef-8da9-57e36ce62f93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(3s+7)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483612} {:answer/id #uuid "4a4e64c9-9d89-58f4-b104-fef2a5ab53b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(2s+7)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483700} {:answer/id #uuid "872747f8-5478-5d1f-be17-16277c421081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(7s+2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483846} {:answer/id #uuid "c3f5b508-c6e2-5175-bc3f-7cda2a58573c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(7s+3)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483954} {:answer/id #uuid "d2c86ffd-4db0-580e-abe6-74afa5106fad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(7s+3)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2c86ffd-4db0-580e-abe6-74afa5106fad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(7s+3)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483989} :answer-field/id #uuid "5473ce96-587f-50c7-8c11-bf336478f1fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484119}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "388f80cd-cabc-537e-b7cd-20f266912f80" :question/math-academy-id "q-111645" :question/problem "Factor the expression $98{s}^{2}+84s+18.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that all of the terms have a common factor of $2.$ Therefore, we can simplify the expression by factoring out $2,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}98{s}^{2}+84s+18 & = \\\\ 2(49{s}^{2}+42s+9)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's factor the expression inside parentheses using the square of a sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}49{s}^{2}+42s+9 & = \\\\ (7s)^{2}+42s+{3}^{2} & = \\\\ (7s)^{2}+2\\cdot (7s\\cdot 3)+{3}^{2} & = \\\\ (7s+3)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our original expression factors as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(49{s}^{2}+42s+9) & = \\\\ 2(7s+3)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484217 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2eca3e6a-417b-5693-8515-2d99ad6c797a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}^{2}{b}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483645} {:answer/id #uuid "4d59ae1e-255c-50cd-afbb-2a6b6c0b6c36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}^{4}{b}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483711} {:answer/id #uuid "552e6aa0-8da1-52b4-ab33-f37479cdfe75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}^{2}{b}^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483720} {:answer/id #uuid "77ad5139-8246-595b-bd68-5063760c5f17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}^{2}{b}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483810} {:answer/id #uuid "e31b4af5-fc25-5e7e-95a9-a2073a37b3dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}^{3}{b}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77ad5139-8246-595b-bd68-5063760c5f17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}^{2}{b}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483810} :answer-field/id #uuid "744ae46d-8d69-511a-b7d4-25e7112917fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484135}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4588ac42-592a-56c9-ba95-db8993497d1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-52309" :question/problem "Simplify $\\sqrt[3]{{a}^{6}{b}^{6}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We write the term under the radical as a perfect cube, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{{a}^{6}{b}^{6}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{a}^{2}{b}^{2}\\cdot {a}^{2}{b}^{2}\\cdot {a}^{2}{b}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{({a}^{2}{b}^{2})}^{3}} & = \\\\ {a}^{2}{b}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484231 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a88e3be-86b1-5646-b222-bbff79557817" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(3x-2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483611} {:answer/id #uuid "9c76dc5d-cdf5-5206-9e60-63b938d2aa3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3(x-4)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483886} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f78be8-45b5-538b-b88a-dead6b1bcfe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9(x+2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483900} {:answer/id #uuid "f3efad0b-d86f-5a94-8f83-37eb2ff02102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3(x-2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484059} {:answer/id #uuid "f9f449cc-10f0-55f1-9b6f-97ae4ad993b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9(x-2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a88e3be-86b1-5646-b222-bbff79557817" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(3x-2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483611} :answer-field/id #uuid "da20f012-448f-53f8-b542-42b6efc9029d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484183}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66f132c4-a82c-5cf3-bd20-df4c38d0e1c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-44099" :question/problem "Factor $-9{x}^{2}+12x-4.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is negative. To reduce the expression to a more familiar form, we can factor out $-1,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9{x}^{2}+12x-4 & = \\\\ -(9{x}^{2}-12x+4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the quadratic expression inside the parentheses using the square of a difference formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}-12x+4 & = \\\\ (3x)^{2}-12x+{2}^{2} & = \\\\ (3x)^{2}-2\\cdot (6x)+{2}^{2} & = \\\\ (3x-2)^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our original expression factors as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(9{x}^{2}-12x+4) & = \\\\ -(3x-2)^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484252 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22f1f4c8-b877-5fac-b542-a40726d7ebe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483628} {:answer/id #uuid "313ddf63-f8de-5a34-8062-2c82d85ce9d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}^{-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483652} {:answer/id #uuid "640a43ab-fe3f-5738-9326-440d23c0350d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}^{1/5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483757} {:answer/id #uuid "b5784a92-2823-5476-a39e-7873e3723fff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{a}^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483929} {:answer/id #uuid "f883a48c-cd87-59cb-8528-5edcfd77629a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22f1f4c8-b877-5fac-b542-a40726d7ebe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483628} :answer-field/id #uuid "845f8a66-1bf3-5ae9-8196-31d024961b81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "95521e10-e107-52c3-9a4a-46859902da66" :question/math-academy-id "q-52491" :question/problem "Simplify $\\sqrt[3]{{a}^{15}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We write the term under the radical as a perfect cube, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{{a}^{15}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{a}^{5}\\cdot {a}^{5}\\cdot {a}^{5}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{({a}^{5})}^{3}} & = \\\\ {a}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484257 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e5d516a-08ba-570d-8dc1-5319b30942d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483863} {:answer/id #uuid "c5101782-6ba9-51e4-a135-77437e019f9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483956} {:answer/id #uuid "ce9eb22e-586f-5330-b915-b57b472e6c22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483983} {:answer/id #uuid "d4bbd9a1-0041-563d-a914-532f0f7cd1d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483992} {:answer/id #uuid "eb97ed63-c199-57e5-8df5-f83c4126e6c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-2x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4bbd9a1-0041-563d-a914-532f0f7cd1d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483992} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a7113b0-a58d-57b5-a47a-af43596f7853" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484152}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a1334155-0338-53af-b4b4-aaee0097bc49" :question/math-academy-id "q-52149" :question/problem "If  $f(x)={x}^{2}+2x-1$ and $g(x)={x}^{2}-x+1,$ then $f(x)+g(x)=$" :question/worked-solution "We put a plus sign between the two polynomials, collect like terms, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)+g(x) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2x-1)+({x}^{2}-x+1) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x-1+{x}^{2}-x+1 & = \\\\ (1+1){x}^{2}+(2-1)x+(-1+1) & = \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+x\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484264 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "379dcf0a-c185-5a50-a270-e4e6a8879659" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt[3]{x+8y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483668} {:answer/id #uuid "39e79e00-bea8-550b-9c7e-df6861afb6f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5(x+8y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483672} {:answer/id #uuid "65e94a43-7480-517b-b5e4-82234a374afc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5(\\sqrt[3]{x}+2\\sqrt[3]{y})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483763} {:answer/id #uuid "73b220af-6c00-51a2-b0e3-663cf13f33a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "125(x+8y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483798} {:answer/id #uuid "7e3a3994-8116-562c-b4db-e7933c0b4358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25(x+2y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39e79e00-bea8-550b-9c7e-df6861afb6f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5(x+8y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483672} :answer-field/id #uuid "547d51e4-47e2-52e7-8dd3-fd09ef7a6abe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484120}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a86cd21a-bd7e-5314-bf81-48804b9affac" :question/math-academy-id "q-82153" :question/problem "Simplify $\\sqrt[3]{125(x+8y)^{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To simplify the expression, we write the term under the radical as a perfect cube, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{125(x+8y)^{3}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{5(x+8y)\\cdot 5(x+8y)\\cdot 5(x+8y)} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{(5(x+8y))}^{3}} & = \\\\ 5(x+8y)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484266 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a41c020-4ee4-5481-b86e-95d2d7b1efb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{(3-x)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483699} {:answer/id #uuid "755dad48-bba6-521d-b6b1-4c1792b0fde6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{(3-x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483804} {:answer/id #uuid "7d3024b4-aff7-5c39-87b9-27adafd22f9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{(3-x)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483821} {:answer/id #uuid "c9e7c6ec-11ff-55ed-94bd-3c2dc2afe7e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{(3-x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483968} {:answer/id #uuid "d5d4928e-8cb5-55fe-95ef-93b9144c043b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{(3-x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5d4928e-8cb5-55fe-95ef-93b9144c043b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{(3-x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483993} :answer-field/id #uuid "68ccab0f-1b29-5cb7-8904-4a9e96752784" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484131}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aff1f300-1ee4-5b20-aeea-457d6b5a90c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-82155" :question/problem "$\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{125}{(3-x)^{3}}}=$" :question/worked-solution "To simplify the expression, we write the term under the radical as a perfect cube, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{125}{(3-x)^{3}}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{5}{(3-x)}\\cdot \\frac{5}{(3-x)}\\cdot \\frac{5}{(3-x)}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{(\\frac{5}{(3-x)})}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{(3-x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484273 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bb8c115-71c8-52fc-b134-d94686e4b9e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{v}^{5}-5{v}^{4}-5{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483816} {:answer/id #uuid "93e1a070-0be2-5ba6-acb7-6112439ed3d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{v}^{5}-5{v}^{4}-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483872} {:answer/id #uuid "97882e12-c84e-5545-b61c-5cf076b14de5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{v}^{5}-5{v}^{3}-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483878} {:answer/id #uuid "e68ebbcb-b8dd-5936-97df-68e5e5d343b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{v}^{4}-5{v}^{3}-5{v}^{2}-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484022} {:answer/id #uuid "ead2d76a-2ace-5594-bd49-b9029b20e0a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{v}^{5}-5{v}^{4}-5{v}^{3}-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ead2d76a-2ace-5594-bd49-b9029b20e0a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{v}^{5}-5{v}^{4}-5{v}^{3}-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484031} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba315b4a-2ca2-5618-87fb-ec19567b9bbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484174}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4fbb5a3-d0b3-5e9d-9d9e-30b9caacb035" :question/math-academy-id "q-111161" :question/problem "Subtract $5{v}^{4}+6{v}^{3}+9$ from $2{v}^{5}+{v}^{3}+2.$" :question/worked-solution "We put a minus sign between the two polynomials, distribute it over the second polynomial, collect like terms, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{v}^{5}+{v}^{3}+2)-(5{v}^{4}+6{v}^{3}+9) & = \\\\ 2{v}^{5}+{v}^{3}+2-5{v}^{4}-6{v}^{3}-9 & = \\\\ 2{v}^{5}-5{v}^{4}+(1-6){v}^{3}+(2-9) & = \\\\ 2{v}^{5}-5{v}^{4}-5{v}^{3}-7 & \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484282 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b48315c-b88d-56e7-9163-6a5e7a7cbe4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{(4k-\\frac{1}{9})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483704} {:answer/id #uuid "648641f9-e71c-5fc8-9d96-1b43ce6d37d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(4k-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483759} {:answer/id #uuid "6c12d1ec-bcf8-590c-8a5a-6919ad803ae9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{(4k-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483774} {:answer/id #uuid "6e7dd96c-e586-5a90-8e07-97c084f41cb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(16k-\\frac{1}{9})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483784} {:answer/id #uuid "9ae55615-aa0b-56be-abe4-4e3656ffeae1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{(16k-\\frac{1}{9})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c12d1ec-bcf8-590c-8a5a-6919ad803ae9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{(4k-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483774} :answer-field/id #uuid "89b397e2-7683-5850-8d9c-30d28cd8ea87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e1247d09-04db-57b2-b09e-dc5dafe32a21" :question/math-academy-id "q-111652" :question/problem "Factor $-16{k}^{2}+\\frac{8}{3}k-\\frac{1}{9}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is negative. To reduce the expression to a more familiar form, we can factor out $-1,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-16{k}^{2}+\\frac{8}{3}k-\\frac{1}{9} & = \\\\ -(16{k}^{2}-\\frac{8}{3}k+\\frac{1}{9})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the quadratic expression inside the parentheses using the square of a difference  formula: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{k}^{2}-\\frac{8}{3}k+\\frac{1}{9} & = \\\\ (4k)^{2}-\\frac{8}{3}k+{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2} & = \\\\ (4k)^{2}-2\\cdot (4k\\cdot \\frac{1}{3})+{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2} & = \\\\ {(4k-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our original expression factors as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(16{k}^{2}-\\frac{8}{3}k+\\frac{1}{9}) & = \\\\ -{(4k-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484292 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "398e9906-9a7d-594a-9e87-6f270ffa1a92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(2m-1)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483671} {:answer/id #uuid "4439d6fb-27f4-5625-aa24-7ff658456c79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(2m+1)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483693} {:answer/id #uuid "51d1d0d6-f508-5bef-a7f1-f1142c1e7206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(4m+1)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483715} {:answer/id #uuid "974b777e-f890-588c-9588-cccf11336c35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4m-1)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483877} {:answer/id #uuid "c2766e46-2765-5512-99cd-6d27f8962334" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2m+1)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4439d6fb-27f4-5625-aa24-7ff658456c79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(2m+1)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483693} :answer-field/id #uuid "0430d0ae-ab49-5bbf-9b16-144277f1be0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484085}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f2d099da-828c-5882-bf9e-a7fe2ace1301" :question/math-academy-id "q-111647" :question/problem "Factor $-4{m}^{2}-4m-1.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is negative. To reduce the expression to a more familiar form, we can factor out $-1,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4{m}^{2}-4m-1 & = \\\\ -(4{m}^{2}+4m+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the quadratic expression inside the parentheses using the square of a sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{m}^{2}+4m+1 & = \\\\ (2m)^{2}+4m+{1}^{2} & = \\\\ (2m)^{2}+2\\cdot (2m\\cdot 1)+{1}^{2} & = \\\\ (2m+1)^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our original expression factors as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(4{m}^{2}+4m+1) & = \\\\ -(2m+1)^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484295 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6b62849-07f9-5df6-9e5f-bb5d41036669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x-\\frac{1}{5})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483959} {:answer/id #uuid "c7b14baa-96be-5e29-b3ca-fac7296e27f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{(2x+\\frac{1}{5})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483961} {:answer/id #uuid "c924f071-a17f-553b-bde2-d655fd8293fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{(x+\\frac{1}{5})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483964} {:answer/id #uuid "db7b288e-4139-5805-81c0-76fbc3968f9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{(x+\\frac{1}{10})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484005} {:answer/id #uuid "ed1478d7-0e89-5af8-bc77-28ddc339e954" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{(4x+\\frac{1}{5})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484037}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7b14baa-96be-5e29-b3ca-fac7296e27f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{(2x+\\frac{1}{5})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483961} :answer-field/id #uuid "57108f3e-71a1-522a-91b8-44b0f9c102f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484123}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fa78e3d6-5bc5-5702-a92b-18645aa6667d" :question/math-academy-id "q-79011" :question/problem "Factor $-4{x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{5}x-\\frac{1}{25}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is negative. To reduce the expression to a more familiar form, we can factor out $-1,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4{x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{5}x-\\frac{1}{25} & = \\\\ -(4{x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{5}x+\\frac{1}{25})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the quadratic expression inside the parentheses using the square of a sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{5}x+\\frac{1}{25} & = \\\\ (2x)^{2}+\\frac{4}{5}x+{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{2} & = \\\\ (2x)^{2}+2\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 2x)+{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{2} & = \\\\ {(2x+\\frac{1}{5})}^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our original expression factors as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(4{x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{5}x+\\frac{1}{25}) & = \\\\ -{(2x+\\frac{1}{5})}^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484297 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-fiel