98 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485138} {:answer/id #uuid "d8fe7281-679d-5b48-bbf3-31ebcfb49f43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485272} {:answer/id #uuid "ef0bc3c0-3c7e-5bb3-b7b5-05ea1ecdb51c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef0bc3c0-3c7e-5bb3-b7b5-05ea1ecdb51c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485328} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1d543d6-08df-55d3-9489-c58386a70208" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b78114a3-4df5-565e-b851-3da12ef84e72" :question/math-academy-id "q-212957" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt{2}}=$" :question/worked-solution "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{2}$ from the denominator, all we need to do is multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{2}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{45}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{45}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we notice that $45$ has a perfect square factor $(9).$ Therefore, we can rewrite $\\sqrt{45}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{45} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{9\\cdot 5} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{5} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify our original fraction as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{45}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{