 and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}}{3} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the product rule to simplify the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{7\\cdot 3}}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{3} & \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485592 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32b1c548-49f0-5278-ade5-87ae9a836c68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{v}^{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484924} {:answer/id #uuid "3cc7469a-4c5a-5c02-a707-a6d244caa391" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484944} {:answer/id #uuid "68550f76-8068-5a20-95d4-041e618def53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485044} {:answer/id #uuid "da946435-d01a-5a40-bc6e-afdd394c6d14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{v}^{16}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485276} {:answer/id #uuid "e9bbb3c6-e4c5-5c33-82a6-4a8eea794f84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cc7469a-4c5a-5c02-a707-a6d244caa391" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484944} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca0326c8-0f04-5e25-9913-33c2c01289fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485452}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "faa7323c-2fa9-5fe0-9081-c51997dba998" :question/math-academy-id "q-104629" :question/problem "Simplify the  expression\n${v}^{9}\\cdot \\frac{{v}^{5}}{{v}^{12}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First we apply the quotient rule, subtracting exponents in the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{v}^{9}\\cdot \\frac{{v}^{5}}{{v}^{12}} & = \\\\ {v}^{9}\\cdot {v}^{5-12} & = \\\\ {v}^{9}\\cdot {v}^{-7} & \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen we apply the product rule, adding exponents in the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{v}^{9}\\cdot {v}^{-7} & = \\\\ {v}^{9+(-7)} & = \\\\ {v}^{9-7} & = \\\\ {v}^{2}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{v}^{9}\\cdot \\frac{{v}^{5}}{{v}^{12}}={v}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485594 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0a31d29-62a3-5603-bc01-bc53d174af98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485165} {:answer/id #uuid "c493ef25-a54b-5081-b9da-7fcaa36128f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\sqrt{5}}{2\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485239} {:answer/id #uuid "eaeace88-26e9-501a-a4b2-7661157c02eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\sqrt{5}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485317} {:answer/id #uuid "ebb79647-6633-5d89-8f8f-9497e10b14c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485319} {:answer/id #uuid "ec09a6b4-86e4-5283-8752-7980712b4e46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eaeace88-26e9-501a-a4b2-7661157c02eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\sqrt{5}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485317} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0e36429-ab7d-5c77-bdcf-ddeb8c1468f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485444}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fc330fed-52a6-53ac-a782-16e92ca6af7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-4397" :question/problem "$\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{5}}=$" :question/worked-solution "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{5}$ from the denominator, we need to multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{5},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{5}} & = \\\\ \\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{5}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}} & = \\\\ \\frac{7\\sqrt{5}}{2(\\sqrt{5})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{7\\sqrt{5}}{2\\cdot 5} & = \\\\ \\frac{7\\sqrt{5}}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487324 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86c09828-8c4b-5bb3-82a8-6bc7c562bf32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "432" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86c09828-8c4b-5bb3-82a8-6bc7c562bf32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "432" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486885} :answer-field/id #uuid "a418d9f4-5901-559b-bb52-77f13f8ff2aa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487233}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4b044a91-329e-59b9-adc9-5aa3764882b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-133796" :question/problem "If $x=20\\,\\text{yd},$ what is the area of Karol's land plot?\n\nArea $\\,=$\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{yd}}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we have to evaluate the polynomial ${x}^{2}+2x-8$ at $x=20.$\n\nSo, we substitute $x=20$ into the polynomial and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x-8 & = \\\\ (20)^{2}+2(20)-8 & = \\\\ 400+40-8 & = \\\\ 432\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area is $432\\,{\\text{yd}}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487379 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fe20cc7-781b-5887-8290-d7c252d770c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fe20cc7-781b-5887-8290-d7c252d770c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486693} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae84797d-d8ce-5c37-8e3b-a77fc43d526c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c5c07663-c2ba-5968-924a-8ce6b0b341c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-133791" :question/problem "Expressed as a polynomial in terms of $x,$ the length of Paul's plot of land is{{field-1}}\nyards." :question/worked-solution "The width of the plot is $x+5$ yards, and its area is $3{x}^{2}+15x$ square yards. Since the $\\text{area}=\\text{length}\\times \\text{width},$ we factor the expression for the area to find the length.\n\nFirst, we find the $\\text{GCF}$ of the two terms:\n\n$$\n\\text{GCF}(3{x}^{2},15x)=3x\n$$\n\nThen, we rewrite each term in the original expression as a product with the $\\text{GCF}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+15x & = \\\\ (3x\\cdot x)+(3x\\cdot 5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we write the $\\text{GCF}$ outside the parentheses and keep the remaining terms inside:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3x\\cdot x)+(3x\\cdot 5) & = \\\\ 3x(x+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we conclude that the length of the plot must be $3x$ yards.\n\n![](images/13/13d17ee1a2e1157f7cf0afa191f2c4096c7c6dea6086f0b3aafd48af159aeb1a.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487383 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5aad4017-2927-590f-958a-30fed270da11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5aad4017-2927-590f-958a-30fed270da11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486796} :answer-field/id #uuid "31779eb9-4392-5feb-93cc-dfac27a0aceb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cbff1985-d682-5038-ad53-7d9761aafbae" :question/math-academy-id "q-133794" :question/problem "![](images/7a/7ad6be914ed14fb22276982edeab75c9726c56e57e32760371db7936b8091468.png)\n\nPaul's neighbor to the south, Karol, has a land plot of area ${x}^{2}+2x-8$ square yards, as shown in the picture. Given that the length of Karol's plot of land is $x+4$ yards, what is the width of the plot in terms of $x?$\n\nKarol's plot width is\n{{field-1}}\nyards." :question/worked-solution "To find the required width, we need to factor the expression ${x}^{2}+2x-8.$\n\nFirst, we find the factor pairs of the constant term $(-8).$ The constant term is negative, so that means one of the factors is negative, and the other is positive:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & \\times (-8) \\\\ (-1) & \\times 8 \\\\ 2 & \\times (-4) \\\\ (-2) & \\times 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find which factor pair adds up to the coefficient of the linear term $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+(-8) & =-7 & \\times  \\\\ -1+8 & =7 & \\times  \\\\ 2+(-4) & =-2 & \\times  \\\\ -2+4 & =2 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the factor pair identified above, write the linear term as $2x=4x-2x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x-8 & ={x}^{2}+4x-2x-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the first two terms and the last two terms separately, and then factor the expression completely:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4x-2x-8 & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}+4x)+(-2x-8) & = \\\\ x(x+4)-2(x+4) & = \\\\ (x-2)(x+4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we conclude that the width must be $x-2$ yards. \n\n![](images/b7/b7bff7b60f02cab37aef8f40d7b303627aedcc37995afc4ffbc2fe756110673a.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487384 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85d2709c-191b-53e9-84d8-9a092328f151" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85d2709c-191b-53e9-84d8-9a092328f151" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486883} :answer-field/id #uuid "30186738-af2f-5bf7-abbc-5cb7b1eb80ab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487157}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cfee4982-2b49-58b3-8a10-a19a8ff05ec4" :question/math-academy-id "q-133793" :question/problem "![](images/c5/c57074e325bd05bdfd076a8f07b50b15c18099fc37bcace725201237d8034a1c.png)\n\nA utility pole is located on the edge of Paul's land, as shown above. The distance from the right edge of Paul's plot to the pole is $2x-4$ yards. Find the distance to the pole from the left edge as a function of $x.$\n\nThe required distance is \n{{field-1}}\nyards." :question/worked-solution "In part 1, we found that the length of Paul's plot is $3x$ yards.\n\nTo find the required distance, we need to subtract polynomials $3x$ and $2x-4:$\n\nWe put a minus sign between the two polynomials, distribute it over the second polynomial, collect like terms, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3x)-(2x-4) & = \\\\ 3x-2x+4 & = \\\\ (3-2)x+4 & = \\\\ x+4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489213 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16272320-c6ad-5fc2-84e3-d7dcf4eeabd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488519} {:answer/id #uuid "6dbec972-4ca4-5309-baad-353d47f0c0b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488685} {:answer/id #uuid "bbb71dd0-6c77-5513-a284-fd4648420655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488847} {:answer/id #uuid "bce6cc9a-4320-5572-bbb9-66f3fdcad111" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488853} {:answer/id #uuid "e7b1499b-0be4-535d-b32e-31dd5753c545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbb71dd0-6c77-5513-a284-fd4648420655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488847} :answer-field/id #uuid "82dc6c2e-5b62-5fbc-aec5-c5800d42bb69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489087}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4b607318-28df-51c2-9737-62f37f3092a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-68934" :question/problem "Evaluate $(-3)\\times ((-8)^{2}\\times \\frac{3}{64}).$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nFirst, consider the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-8)^{2}\\times \\frac{3}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying PEMDAS to this expression, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-8)^{2}\\times \\frac{3}{64} & = \\\\ 64\\times \\frac{3}{64} & = \\\\ \\frac{64}{1}\\times \\frac{3}{64} & = \\\\ \\frac{64\\times 3}{1\\times 64} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{64}\\times 3}{1\\times \\cancel{64}} & = \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)\\times ((-8)^{2}\\times \\frac{3}{64}) & = \\\\ (-3)\\times 3 & = \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489218 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a709506-d82a-59b7-a2b1-cc2efb6ccd0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488527} {:answer/id #uuid "27225eb8-4e94-5553-b530-1190a04b98a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488552} {:answer/id #uuid "5b6eb62b-0638-56b2-a12d-831896cfe037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488646} {:answer/id #uuid "b2519c59-5675-54f8-9c49-fb9bd709992d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488827} {:answer/id #uuid "fb6ce3ab-bbde-5378-b4f8-47c8bd713822" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{120}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27225eb8-4e94-5553-b530-1190a04b98a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488552} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb165dbd-4e64-57b9-b591-6886c0a643cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "50989de1-e6f3-5831-87a9-51e32375a2a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-68926" :question/problem "Calculate $(\\frac{2}{5}\\times {(-5)}^{2})÷({(-2)}^{5}-(-20)).$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nFirst, we consider the expressions inside each of the parentheses. The first one is.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}\\times {(-5)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying PEMDAS to this expression, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}\\times {(-5)}^{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}\\times 25 & = \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}\\times \\frac{25}{1} & = \\\\ \\frac{2\\times 25}{5\\times 1} & = \\\\ \\frac{50}{5} & = \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe expression inside the second parentheses is.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(-2)}^{5}-(-20).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying PEMDAS to this expression, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(-2)}^{5}-(-20) & = \\\\ (-32)+20 & = \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{2}{5}\\times {(-5)}^{2})÷({(-2)}^{5}-(-20)) & = \\\\ 10÷(-12) & = \\\\ \\frac{10}{(-12)} & = \\\\ -\\frac{10}{12} & = \\\\ -\\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489220 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ad97cff-9e2e-563f-b6a9-474cb218d7b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+6y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488561} {:answer/id #uuid "3b3b0a0d-ced6-5f22-a4fb-24960d846e07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8x+8y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488593} {:answer/id #uuid "c4a42675-06f0-5aac-910b-a636d62f1f43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x+6y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488868} {:answer/id #uuid "f3da4469-9b3d-59cb-947a-65e2c706782e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x+9y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488984} {:answer/id #uuid "f668a967-ab29-563f-b04a-57e4cb7a86bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+9y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4a42675-06f0-5aac-910b-a636d62f1f43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x+6y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488868} :answer-field/id #uuid "a999e85d-466d-5b48-8784-0835d63fcc46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489109}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "56c7326b-73aa-516e-8094-38a5a4c858fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-141910" :question/problem "$(-2)(3x+y)+8y=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we distribute the $(-2)$ over each of the terms in parentheses.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}(-2)(3x+y)+8y & = \\\\ (-2)\\cdot 3x+(-2)\\cdot y+8y & = \\\\ (-6x)+(-2y)+8y & = \\\\ -6x-2y+8y & \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we collect like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-6x-2y+8y & = \\\\ -6x+(8y-2y) & = \\\\ -6x+6y & \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489221 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05bb9e95-1d10-5069-a452-c7b0b169db9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-4a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488483} {:answer/id #uuid "5ae65b8c-35be-548c-a00d-0cc258220579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20-4a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488644} {:answer/id #uuid "a6e3c89e-98d3-5561-a67a-a1b501b72224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488803} {:answer/id #uuid "cb99c864-e94b-5f43-b916-b054dd2ef046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20-a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488884} {:answer/id #uuid "fa49a3a2-0170-50ed-940e-118d1bf5b6a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-4a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ae65b8c-35be-548c-a00d-0cc258220579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20-4a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488644} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcc25ce6-564a-5da0-94c0-553cbcb50892" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489167}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5d0b6029-5d16-5038-805d-6574595234a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-141938" :question/problem "Simplify $4(2-a)+12.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we distribute the $4$ over each of the terms in parentheses.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2-a)+12 & = \\\\ 4\\cdot 2+4\\cdot (-a)+12 & = \\\\ (8)+(-4a)+12 & = \\\\ 8-4a+12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we collect like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-4a+12 & = \\\\ (8+12)-4a & = \\\\ 20-4a\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489266 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ac84694-db3c-508f-ab4f-56602c4d7c88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ac84694-db3c-508f-ab4f-56602c4d7c88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488643} :answer-field/id #uuid "36634756-bd5b-5b68-9066-c998674fe2a6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ide